{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Until Nahal Eshkol.</b> Rashi explains: this teaches that four craftsmen walked in it, two warp and two woof, as stated in [the chapter] HaSocher et HaPo'alim. Workers, on their way out, eat from the grapes from one craftsman's row to the next; and on their return, from the winepress — i.e., from row to row."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:17.026686872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}